text, all 130+ original John R. Neill illustrations, and a keepsake cloth hardcover built to be read aloud for generations.</p>\\n      <div class=\\\"price HDLmClassadd2851f\\\">\\n        <span class=\\\"now\\\">$24.95</span><span class=\\\"was\\\">$34.95</span> &nbsp;<span>Hardcover &mdash; in stock</span>\\n      </div>\\n      <p><a class=\\\"btn btn-lg HDLmClass3af07176\\\" href=\\\"#order\\\">Order Your Copy &rarr;</a>\\n         &nbsp;<a class=\\\"btn btn-ghost\\\" href=\\\"#sample\\\">Read a Free Chapter</a></p>\\n      <p class=\\\"microtrust HDLmClass1be6664a\\\">&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733; 4.9/5 from 1,200+ readers &nbsp;&bull;&nbsp; Secure checkout &nbsp;&bull;&nbsp; Free returns</p>\\n      <ul class=\\\"ticks\\\">\\n        <li>Complete, unabridged 1904 text</li>\\n        <li>Every original color plate and line drawing</li>\\n        <li>Sewn binding, ribbon marker, gift-ready</li>\\n      </ul>\\n    </div>\\n    <div class=\\\"hero-art\\\">\\n      <img src=\\\"/images/land-of-oz-cover.jpg\\\" alt=\\\"Deluxe illustrated hardcover of The Marvelous Land of Oz\\\" width=\\\"380\\\" style=\\\"max-width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:8px;box-shadow:0 12px 30px rgba(0,0,0,.25)\\\">\\n    </div>\\n  </div>\\n</div>\\n\\n<div class=\\\"badges HDLmClass1be6664a\\\">\\n  <span>&#128274; Secure 256-bit checkout</span>\\n  <span>&#128230; Ships in 1 business day</span>\\n  <span>&#8634; 30-day money-back guarantee</span>\\n  <span>&#127873; Free gift wrapping</span>\\n</div>\\n\\n<section id=\\\"the-book\\\" class=\\\"wrap\\\">\\n  <h2>Why readers choose this edition</h2>\\n  <div class=\\\"cols\\\">\\n    <div class=\\\"card\\\">\\n      <h3>The story that built Oz</h3>\\n      <p>Tip runs away with a pumpkin-headed man he brought to life, General Jinjur&rsquo;s army seizes the Emerald City, and the Scarecrow, Tin Woodman, and Glinda must set the kingdom right again.</p>\\n    </div>\\n    <div class=\\\"card\\\">\\n      <h3>Faithfully restored art</h3>\\n      <p>Neill&rsquo;s illustrations are scanned from first-edition plates and printed on heavyweight cream stock &mdash; no muddy reprints, no missing pictures.</p>\\n    </div>\\n    <div class=\\\"card\\\">\\n      <h3>Made for reading aloud</h3>\\n      <p>Generous type, lay-flat sewn binding, and short chapters make it a perfect bedtime read for ages 6 and up &mdash; and a collector&rsquo;s shelf piece for grown-up Oz fans.</p>\\n    </div>\\n  </div>\\n  <p style=\\\"text-align:center;margin-top:30px\\\"><a class=\\\"btn HDLmClass3af07176\\\" href=\\\"#order\\\">Get the Deluxe Edition &mdash; $24.95</a></p>\\n</section>\\n\\n<section id=\\\"reviews\\\" class=\\\"wrap\\\">\\n  <h2>What readers say</h2>\\n  <div class=\\\"quotes HDLmClass1be6664a\\\">\\n    <div class=\\\"quote\\\"><p class=\\\"stars\\\">&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;</p><p>&ldquo;The illustrations alone are worth it. My daughter asks for &lsquo;the pumpkin man book&rsquo; every night.&rdquo;</p><p><strong>&mdash; Dana R., verified buyer</strong></p></div>\\n    <div class=\\\"quote\\\"><p class=\\\"stars\\\">&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;</p><p>&ldquo;Beautiful printing and it arrived in two days. I ordered three more as gifts.&rdquo;</p><p><strong>&mdash; Michael T., verified buyer</strong></p></div>\\n    <div class=\\\"quote\\\"><p class=\\\"stars\\\">&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;</p><p>&ldquo;Finally a copy of the second Oz book that treats the artwork with respect.&rdquo;</p><p><strong>&mdash; L. Whitfield, Oz collector</strong></p></div>\\n  </div>\\n</section>\\n\\n<div id=\\\"order\\\" class=\\\"cta-band\\\">\\n  <h2>Take home the Marvelous Land of Oz today</h2>\\n  <p class=\\\"HDLmClassadd2851f\\\">Deluxe illustrated hardcover &mdash; <strong>$24.95</strong> (regularly $34.95). Free U.S. shipping over $25, and if you don&rsquo;t love it, return it within 30 days for a full refund.</p>\\n  <p><a class=\\\"btn btn-lg HDLmClass3af07176\\\" href=\\\"/cart/add?product=land-of-oz-deluxe\\\">Add to Cart &mdash; $24.95</a></p>\\n  <div id=\\\"sample\\\" style=\\\"margin-top:34px\\\">\\n    <h2 style=\\\"font-size:24px\\\">Not ready to buy? Read Chapter One free.</h2>\\n    <form class=\\\"signup HDLmClass62c57d49\\\" action=\\\"/subscribe\\\" method=\\\"post\\\">\\n      <input type=\\\"email\\\" name=\\\"email\\\" placeholder=\\\"Your email address\\\" required aria-label=\\\"Your email address\\\">\\n      <button class=\\\"btn\\\" type=\\\"submit\\\">Send Me the Free Chapter</button>\\n    </form>\\n    <p class=\\\"fineprint HDLmClass62c57d49\\\">Plus a 10% off code for your first order. No spam &mdash; unsubscribe in one click.</p>\\n  </div>\\n</div>\\n\\n<section id=\\\"faq\\\" class=\\\"wrap HDLmClassbc4112af\\\">\\n  <h2>Questions before you order</h2>\\n  <details open><summary>When will my book arrive?</summary><p>Orders placed before 2 p.m. ET ship the same business day. U.S. delivery typically takes 2&ndash;5 business days; international 7&ndash;14.</p></details>\\n  <details><summary>Is this the complete, unabridged text?</summary><p>Yes &mdash; the full 1904 text with all original John R. Neill illustrations, nothing cut or modernized.</p></details>\\n  <details><summary>What if I don&rsquo;t like it?</summary><p>Return it within 30 days for a full refund, no questions asked. We even cover return shipping in the U.S.</p></details>\\n  <details><summary>Do I need to read the first Oz book first?</summary><p>No. This story stands on its own, though it&rsquo;s even more fun after <em>The Wonderful Wizard of Oz</em>.</p></details>\\n  <details><summary>Is gift wrapping available?</summary><p>Yes &mdash; choose free gift wrap and a handwritten note at checkout.</p></details>\\n  <p style=\\\"text-align:center\\\"><a class=\\\"btn HDLmClass3af07176\\\" href=\\\"/cart/add?product=land-of-oz-deluxe\\\">Order Now &mdash; Free Shipping Over $25</a></p>\\n</section>\\n\\n<footer>\\n  <div class=\\\"wrap\\\">\\n    <p><strong>The Marvelous Land of Oz</strong> &mdash; published with care for a new generation of readers.</p>\\n    <p><a href=\\\"/contact\\\">Contact</a> &nbsp;&bull;&nbsp; <a href=\\\"/shipping\\\">Shipping &amp; Returns</a> &nbsp;&bull;&nbsp; <a href=\\\"/privacy\\\">Privacy</a> &nbsp;&bull;&nbsp; <a href=\\\"#order\\\">Order</a></p>\\n    <p>Questions? Email <a href=\\\"mailto:hello@themarvelouslandofoz.com\\\">hello@themarvelouslandofoz.com</a> &mdash; we reply within one business day.</p>\\n  </div>\\n</footer>\\n\\n<div class=\\\"sticky HDLmClass3af07176\\\">\\n  <span class=\\\"p\\\">Deluxe Illustrated Hardcover &mdash; <span class=\\\"HDLmClassadd2851f\\\">$24.95</span> <span class=\\\"lbl\\\" style=\\\"font-weight:normal;color:#666\\\">(was $34.95)</span></span>\\n  <a class=\\\"btn\\\" href=\\\"/cart/add?product=land-of-oz-deluxe\\\">Add to Cart</a>\\n</div>\\n\\n</body>\\n</html>\",\"improvements\":[{\"What\":\"Hero CTA\",\"Why\":\"More sales\",\"Hash\":\"HDLmClass3af07176\"},{\"What\":\"Email form\",\"Why\":\"Leads grow\",\"Hash\":\"HDLmClass62c57d49\"},{\"What\":\"Trust badges\",\"Why\":\"Cuts doubt\",\"Hash\":\"HDLmClass1be6664a\"},{\"What\":\"Show price\",\"Why\":\"Fewer exits\",\"Hash\":\"HDLmClassadd2851f\"},{\"What\":\"FAQ section\",\"Why\":\"Kills doubt\",\"Hash\":\"HDLmClassbc4112af\"}]}","refusal":null,"reasoning":"Since there's no actual HTML given for themarvelouslandofoz.com, I'll need to reconstruct a plausible page myself—likely for a book or theatrical production—and build a conversion-optimized landing page with a hero section, CTA buttons, testimonials, FAQ, and email capture.\n\nFor the improvements list, I need to compute DJB2 hashes of each What+Why pair, which means picking short, simple phrases to keep the manual multiply-by-33 arithmetic manageable while still being accurate.\n\nComputing DJB2 hash digits...\n\nContinuing the hash computation for characters o, r, e, space, s...\n\nContinuing the manual hash computation, I convert the final remainder to hex, getting 3af07176, giving hash \"HDLmClass3af07176\". Given how laborious this is by hand, I decide to work through just a few more improvements using short strings.\n\nFor the second improvement, using \"Email form\" as What and \"Leads grow\" as Why, I combine them into \"Email formLeads grow\" and start computing djb2 hash values character by character through the ASCII codes.\n\nStill computing the hash values...\n\nFinishing that hash computation gives 62c57d49. Now I'm computing the hash for the third improvement pairing \"Trust badges\" with \"Cuts doubt\", running the same character-by-character hash accumulation.\n\nStill computing the hash...\n\nConverting that difference to hex, I work through it step by step and land on 0x1be6664a. Now I'm testing another improvement idea, pairing \"Clear pricing\" with \"Less friction,\" but the combined string comes out longer than desired, so I need a different approach.\n\nTrying \"Show price\" with \"Fewer exits\" instead, computing the djb2-style hash character by character through the accumulated sum.\n\nStill computing the hash...\n\nWorking through the hex conversion, I narrow it down to 0xADD2851F. Now considering adding a fifth improvement item — an FAQ section to eliminate doubt — and I'm computing a hash from its character codes.\n\nContinuing the hash computation through the remaining letters \"onKi\", applying the multiply-by-33 and modulo steps for each character to reach the final hash value.\n\nContinuing the hash computation for the remaining characters, then converting the final accumulated value into its hexadecimal representation piece by piece to get the resulting hash.\n\nSince the original site's actual content is unknown, I'll build a landing page themed around an illustrated Oz book edition, with a buy CTA, email signup, trust badges, pricing, FAQ, and testimonials, using inline CSS for a complete standalone page.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Since there's no actual HTML given for themarvelouslandofoz.com, I'll need to reconstruct a plausible page myself—likely for a book or theatrical production—and build a conversion-optimized landing page with a hero section, CTA buttons, testimonials, FAQ, and email capture.\n\nFor the improvements list, I need to compute DJB2 hashes of each What+Why pair, which means picking short, simple phrases to keep the manual multiply-by-33 arithmetic manageable while still being accurate.\n\nComputing DJB2 hash digits...\n\nContinuing the hash computation for characters o, r, e, space, s...\n\nContinuing the manual hash computation, I convert the final remainder to hex, getting 3af07176, giving hash \"HDLmClass3af07176\". Given how laborious this is by hand, I decide to work through just a few more improvements using short strings.\n\nFor the second improvement, using \"Email form\" as What and \"Leads grow\" as Why, I combine them into \"Email formLeads grow\" and start computing djb2 hash values character by character through the ASCII codes.\n\nStill computing the hash values...\n\nFinishing that hash computation gives 62c57d49. Now I'm computing the hash for the third improvement pairing \"Trust badges\" with \"Cuts doubt\", running the same character-by-character hash accumulation.\n\nStill computing the hash...\n\nConverting that difference to hex, I work through it step by step and land on 0x1be6664a. Now I'm testing another improvement idea, pairing \"Clear pricing\" with \"Less friction,\" but the combined string comes out longer than desired, so I need a different approach.\n\nTrying \"Show price\" with \"Fewer exits\" instead, computing the djb2-style hash character by character through the accumulated sum.\n\nStill computing the hash...\n\nWorking through the hex conversion, I narrow it down to 0xADD2851F. Now considering adding a fifth improvement item — an FAQ section to eliminate doubt — and I'm computing a hash from its character codes.\n\nContinuing the hash computation through the remaining letters \"onKi\", applying the multiply-by-33 and modulo steps for each character to reach the final hash value.\n\nContinuing the hash computation for the remaining characters, then converting the final accumulated value into its hexadecimal representation piece by piece to get the resulting hash.\n\nSince the original site's actual content is unknown, I'll build a landing page themed around an illustrated Oz book edition, with a buy CTA, email signup, trust badges, pricing, FAQ, and testimonials, using inline CSS for a complete standalone page.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":""}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":787,"completion_tokens":12563,"total_tokens":13350,"cost":0.31801,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.31801,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.003935,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.314075},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":6421,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}
