class=\\\"btn btn-primary\\\" href=\\\"01.htm\\\">Start reading Book 1 &rarr;</a>\\n        <a class=\\\"btn btn-ghost\\\" href=\\\"#books\\\">See all 14 books</a>\\n      </div>\\n      <p class=\\\"reassure\\\">Free &middot; No signup &middot; No download &middot; Works on phone, tablet &amp; desktop</p>\\n    </div>\\n  </div>\\n</header>\\n\\n<div class=\\\"trust HDLmClass5d92ab17\\\">\\n  <div class=\\\"wrap\\\">\\n    <ul>\\n      <li>14 complete novels</li>\\n      <li>Published 1900&ndash;1920</li>\\n      <li>Public domain &ndash; always free</li>\\n      <li>Read in your browser</li>\\n    </ul>\\n  </div>\\n</div>\\n\\n<section id=\\\"books\\\" class=\\\"HDLmClass3e8b62d9\\\">\\n  <div class=\\\"wrap\\\">\\n    <h2>Read the Oz books in order</h2>\\n    <p class=\\\"sub\\\">Tap any title to begin reading instantly. Baum's 14 numbered novels are listed in original publication order, with two bonus works included.</p>\\n    <ul class=\\\"books\\\">\\n      <li class=\\\"book featured\\\"><a href=\\\"01.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">1</span><span><span class=\\\"title\\\">The Wonderful Wizard of Oz</span><span class=\\\"meta\\\">1900 &middot; The story that started it all</span><span class=\\\"flag\\\">Best place to start</span></span></a></li>\\n      <li class=\\\"book extra\\\"><a href=\\\"OzPlay.pdf\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">PDF</span><span><span class=\\\"title\\\">The Wizard of Oz: A Dramatic Composition</span><span class=\\\"meta\\\">1902 &middot; Stage play &middot; PDF</span></span></a></li>\\n      <li class=\\\"book\\\"><a href=\\\"02.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">2</span><span><span class=\\\"title\\\">The Marvelous Land of Oz</span><span class=\\\"meta\\\">1904</span></span></a></li>\\n      <li class=\\\"book\\\"><a href=\\\"03.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">3</span><span><span class=\\\"title\\\">Ozma of Oz</span><span class=\\\"meta\\\">1907</span></span></a></li>\\n      <li class=\\\"book\\\"><a href=\\\"04.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">4</span><span><span class=\\\"title\\\">Dorothy and the Wizard in Oz</span><span class=\\\"meta\\\">1908</span></span></a></li>\\n      <li class=\\\"book\\\"><a href=\\\"05.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">5</span><span><span class=\\\"title\\\">The Road to Oz</span><span class=\\\"meta\\\">1909</span></span></a></li>\\n      <li class=\\\"book\\\"><a href=\\\"06.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">6</span><span><span class=\\\"title\\\">The Emerald City of Oz</span><span class=\\\"meta\\\">1910</span></span></a></li>\\n      <li class=\\\"book\\\"><a href=\\\"07.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">7</span><span><span class=\\\"title\\\">The Patchwork Girl of Oz</span><span class=\\\"meta\\\">1913</span></span></a></li>\\n      <li class=\\\"book extra\\\"><a href=\\\"08.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">Bonus</span><span><span class=\\\"title\\\">Little Wizard Stories of Oz</span><span class=\\\"meta\\\">1913 &middot; Six short stories</span></span></a></li>\\n      <li class=\\\"book\\\"><a href=\\\"09.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">8</span><span><span class=\\\"title\\\">Tik-Tok of Oz</span><span class=\\\"meta\\\">1914</span></span></a></li>\\n      <li class=\\\"book\\\"><a href=\\\"10.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">9</span><span><span class=\\\"title\\\">The Scarecrow of Oz</span><span class=\\\"meta\\\">1915</span></span></a></li>\\n      <li class=\\\"book\\\"><a href=\\\"11.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">10</span><span><span class=\\\"title\\\">Rinkitink in Oz</span><span class=\\\"meta\\\">1916</span></span></a></li>\\n      <li class=\\\"book\\\"><a href=\\\"12.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">11</span><span><span class=\\\"title\\\">The Lost Princess of Oz</span><span class=\\\"meta\\\">1917</span></span></a></li>\\n      <li class=\\\"book\\\"><a href=\\\"13.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">12</span><span><span class=\\\"title\\\">The Tin Woodman of Oz</span><span class=\\\"meta\\\">1918</span></span></a></li>\\n      <li class=\\\"book\\\"><a href=\\\"14.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">13</span><span><span class=\\\"title\\\">The Magic of Oz</span><span class=\\\"meta\\\">1919</span></span></a></li>\\n      <li class=\\\"book\\\"><a href=\\\"15.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">14</span><span><span class=\\\"title\\\">Glinda of Oz</span><span class=\\\"meta\\\">1920 &middot; Baum's final Oz novel</span></span></a></li>\\n    </ul>\\n  </div>\\n</section>\\n\\n<section class=\\\"HDLmClass6c47d10e\\\">\\n  <div class=\\\"wrap\\\">\\n    <div class=\\\"search-box\\\">\\n      <h2>Search the Oz books</h2>\\n      <p class=\\\"sub\\\">Looking for a character, a place or a favorite scene? Search every book on this site.</p>\\n      <form class=\\\"search-form\\\" action=\\\"https://www.google.com/cse\\\" method=\\\"get\\\" role=\\\"search\\\">\\n        <input type=\\\"hidden\\\" name=\\\"cx\\\" value=\\\"002807121847390519013:ddj9f84mdsw\\\" />\\n        <input type=\\\"hidden\\\" name=\\\"ie\\\" value=\\\"UTF-8\\\" />\\n        <label for=\\\"ozq\\\" style=\\\"position:absolute;left:-9999px;\\\">Search the Oz books</label>\\n        <input id=\\\"ozq\\\" type=\\\"text\\\" name=\\\"q\\\" size=\\\"31\\\" placeholder=\\\"e.g. Dorothy, Emerald City, Tin Woodman\\\" />\\n        <input type=\\\"submit\\\" name=\\\"sa\\\" value=\\\"Search\\\" />\\n      </form>\\n    </div>\\n  </div>\\n</section>\\n\\n<section class=\\\"footer-cta HDLmClass2f5e9c84\\\">\\n  <div class=\\\"wrap\\\">\\n    <h2>Ready to go back to Oz?</h2>\\n    <p class=\\\"sub\\\">Begin with the original 1900 classic, or jump straight to the second adventure.</p>\\n    <div class=\\\"btns\\\" style=\\\"justify-content:center;\\\">\\n      <a class=\\\"btn btn-primary\\\" href=\\\"01.htm\\\">Read The Wonderful Wizard of Oz &rarr;</a>\\n      <a class=\\\"btn btn-ghost\\\" style=\\\"color:var(--emerald-dark);border-color:var(--emerald);\\\" href=\\\"02.htm\\\">Read Book 2</a>\\n    </div>\\n  </div>\\n</section>\\n\\n<footer>\\n  <div class=\\\"wrap\\\">\\n    <p>The Oz books of L. Frank Baum (1856&ndash;1919) are in the public domain and free for everyone to read.</p>\\n  </div>\\n</footer>\\n\\n<script type=\\\"text/javascript\\\" src=\\\"https://www.google.com/coop/cse/brand?form=cse-search-box&lang=en\\\"></script>\\n</body>\\n</html>\",\"improvements\":[{\"What\":\"Added a hero section with a clear headline, value proposition and a primary call-to-action button (\\\"Start reading Book 1\\\"), built around the existing Cowardly Lion image with descriptive alt text.\",\"Why\":\"The original page opened with a bare image and an unlabeled list, giving visitors no direction. A single prominent CTA plus a benefit-led headline tells people exactly what they can do next, which lifts click-through into the books.\",\"Hash\":\"HDLmClass7a1c4f3b\"},{\"What\":\"Added a reassurance/trust bar stating 14 complete novels, publication range, public-domain status and browser reading.\",\"Why\":\"Removing uncertainty about cost, signup and availability reduces bounce and increases the share of visitors who start reading.\",\"Hash\":\"HDLmClass5d92ab17\"},{\"What\":\"Converted the plain link list into a responsive card grid with numbered badges, publication years, a highlighted \\\"Best place to start\\\" card for the 1900 original, and corrected the typo \\\"Wixard\\\" to \\\"Wizard\\\".\",\"Why\":\"Large tappable cards with visual hierarchy and correct spelling improve scannability, mobile usability and credibility, all of which raise engagement with the book links.\",\"Hash\":\"HDLmClass3e8b62d9\"},{\"What\":\"Repaired the search feature by wrapping the inputs in a real form that submits to the Google Custom Search endpoint, keeping the original cx and ie values, and added a label, placeholder and styled search button.\",\"Why\":\"The original inputs had no form element, so searching was impossible; a working, inviting search box helps visitors find content instead of leaving.\",\"Hash\":\"HDLmClass6c47d10e\"},{\"What\":\"Added a closing call-to-action section repeating the main reading links after the list, plus a short public-domain footer note.\",\"Why\":\"Visitors who scroll to the bottom are given an immediate next step instead of a dead end, capturing conversions that would otherwise be lost.\",\"Hash\":\"HDLmClass2f5e9c84\"},{\"What\":\"Modernized the document to HTML5 with a mobile viewport meta tag, charset, SEO title and meta description, and a complete responsive stylesheet with readable typography.\",\"Why\":\"Mobile-friendly, fast-reading pages with descriptive titles attract more organic traffic and keep visitors on the page, directly increasing conversions.\",\"Hash\":\"HDLmClass4b8d37f6\"}]}","refusal":null,"reasoning":"Since no specific changes were requested, I'll decide on my own improvements while preserving all original scripts, links, and images. I'm planning a redesigned page with better styling, a hero section, book cards, a fixed search form linked to Google CSE, a typo correction from \"Wixard\" to \"Wizard,\" and responsive mobile design. I also need to compute DJB2 hashes manually for the content verification.\n\nI'll skip the newsletter form idea since there's no backend, and instead focus on a \"Continue reading\" CTA and highlighting the PDF download, plus better meta tags for SEO. For the search form, I'll wire it to Google's CSE endpoint with the original cx value so it actually works, and I'll upgrade the doctype to HTML5 while keeping the existing scripts intact.\n\nWriting the HTML document...\n\nWriting CSS styles...","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Since no specific changes were requested, I'll decide on my own improvements while preserving all original scripts, links, and images. I'm planning a redesigned page with better styling, a hero section, book cards, a fixed search form linked to Google CSE, a typo correction from \"Wixard\" to \"Wizard,\" and responsive mobile design. I also need to compute DJB2 hashes manually for the content verification.\n\nI'll skip the newsletter form idea since there's no backend, and instead focus on a \"Continue reading\" CTA and highlighting the PDF download, plus better meta tags for SEO. For the search form, I'll wire it to Google's CSE endpoint with the original cx value so it actually works, and I'll upgrade the doctype to HTML5 while keeping the existing scripts intact.\n\nWriting the HTML document...\n\nWriting CSS styles...","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":""}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":3047,"completion_tokens":8501,"total_tokens":11548,"cost":0.22776,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.22776,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.015235,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.212525},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1295,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}
